## Context

The [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review) found separate parser and form-hint causes in one ticket. Subject-only matching concealed that distinction. The executable dedupe explorer already compares tenant-specific causes instead of subjects.

## Proposed decision

Replace the operational rule in [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) with evidence-based matching: check tenant locale, booking form, channel and reported behavior before merging. Use subject similarity for discovery, not proof. Deduplicate export rows by report ID independently of merging related reports into a ticket.

## Consequences

The desk must read enough evidence to distinguish causes. Unknown cases remain visibly unresolved. Existing accepted decisions are not rewritten; this proposal requires desk acceptance before it replaces their policy.

